# Naming

Shared suffixes: `Entity`, `Dto`, `Mapper`, `Api`, `RemoteDataSource`, `LocalDataSource`, `Repository`, `RepositoryImpl`, `UseCase`, `Page`, `State`.

Stack suffix (Riverpod only — see `state-management.mdc`):

- `ViewModel` (the class **is** the `Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier`)

```dart
// BAD
class HttpFailure {}
class MyCourseCard extends StatelessWidget {} // feature widget

// GOOD
class CoursesViewModel extends AsyncNotifier<CoursesState> {}
```

- The eleven Failure types in `lib/core/errors/failures/failure.dart` are the only ones. Spell `HttpErrorFailure`, never `HttpFailure`. Do not add a new subtype.
- Prefix `my_` / `My` is only for the four shared design-system widgets: `MyDialog`, `MySnackbar`, `MyEmptyState`, `MyInlineError`. Feature widgets use the feature name.
- Never ship two controllers for one screen (`ViewModel` + `Notifier`).
- Session owner: `authSessionProvider`. Do not invent `authStateProvider` or `AuthCubit`.
- User-facing strings: add the same key to `lib/core/translations/l10n/app_en.arb` and `app_ar.arb`. Read via `context.tr`. Locale switching uses the stack's locale owner (`localeProvider` or `LocaleCubit`). Never `AppLocalizations.of(context)` and never hardcode UI copy.
- Routes live in `AppRoutes`. Endpoints live in `AppEndpoints`.
